@everyone Rough day and evening yesterday.. recap:

Ov Fla st I didn’t consider or weight enough the idea that Fla st could pull away and then no late fouls and less chance to go over, prob not the best bet..ov 1h Indiana st very easy W..ov 1h Albany wasn’t even close just died..ov 1h tt Va tech was pretty rough we just couldn’t score last 2 mins..un gw was a really tough beat w the game sitting on 1 w 32 sec left and the team trailing dribbling up court w a buncha points to give, then even w that sillyness w 6 sec left gw had ball under their own hoop down 3 and a typical last sec 3 usually misses and we win, nope..Idaho st 1h over was sailing to an easy win and completely died the last 8 mins..ov 1h mia was easy even w a million missed fts..ov Idaho st full game pretty easy W..ov 1h s Illinois was a little dicey but pulled away late for us..ov 1h Delaware lost and a buncha of missed one and ones really hurt..northridge -5.5 was a bad read they just couldn’t get stops..ucf cfb ml wins easy..ov Princeton was flying and almost impossible to lose somehow it loses and Monmouth doesn’t foul down 8 in last mins very rough beat.. ov 1h tt Pitt and ov 1h were easy..ov Pitt full game also was very easy..wisc +10.5 they pulled to within 8 i think maybe even 6 and seemed to have all the momentum only to completely collapse in the last 8 mins..ov n Tex i split w the ov155.5 piece winning and the ov157.5 piece losing..ov 1h e Carolina was pretty straight forward tons of fouls..ov vandy got there but their tt didn’t so we split out unfortunately.. (edited)
Saturday, November 21, 2026 at 10:14 AM

@everyone un tulsa was a bet on miss st D not allowing easy hoops late and they didn’t allow much and we barely squeezed it out..ov Campbell i felt we deserved to win and k st wasting from 52 sec to 30 before fouling i think cost us what seemed to be looking like a W..ov boise i felt a big fave trailing would not give up and that came to fruition but we were very fortunate..ov 1h tt Fresno i lost both pieces somehow..Fresno -13.5 we led by 18 and i thought we just pull away but nope endless turnovers in the last 3 mins doomed what coulda been a W..new Mex -.5 3q cfb was very lucky as they didn’t overturn the td when the guy was clearly short on 4th down and goal..ov 1h stmarys needed 18 in last 4.30 which put us very slightly ahead but then 2 mins empty after scoring 68 in the first 15.5 mins and down the drain we go..
In total I think I deserved better yesterday(there were a few lucky occasions, but there were prob double the rough/bad beats) overall prob deserved to be around even maybe down a tiny amt.. (edited)
Saturday, November 21, 2026 at 10:14 AM

@everyone recap
Yesterday was a microcosm of my CFB season from Hell..
Siena un cbb was a classic mistake that I usually don’t make anymore and that is betting at the 1st (under 16 min) timeout, not sure I woulda saved myself from this but possibly might have and then almost def would have been on 1h over at some point later in the half. So just a colossal screw up to start the day..un unc Greensboro cbb I thought we may get a classic slow game w a fave leading by 15-20 and keeping score low, it was wrong from the jump..un tt det mercy, Mich st can smother these weak teams defensively esp at home see the 1h scores in some of their blowouts. And after the loss they had the other day I was looking for it, coupla lucky 3s and we lose, the pace was a bit too fast tho so I deserved the loss..neb cfb I knew in my bones neb was right and after I saw they could move the ball I was in..ov 1h wvu pushed the 45 but I lose the ov47.5 when after scoring 45 already and 3.40 left nobody scores and a kicker doinks a long fg, just the 1st in a long line of keister blasts in cfb yesterday..
